#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:5
#: 9d44ac399cae457fae07634e3f13ea63
msgid "Log Analysis Case Study: Turn Rate Adjustment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:7
#: a2bb94b5d17d4f8fbdc2ecfce2c3fd54
msgid "Analyzing flight logs can help you diagnose problems with your missions. This case study brings you an example of a flight where, by analyzing the log data, our resident expert, Andrew Tridgell, suggested adjusting the turn rate and increasing the maximum roll angle to correct the plane's failure to reach a waypoint as a result of turning too slowly. The original forum posts can be found `**here** <https://diydrones.com/forum/topics/arduplane-2-73-released?commentId=705844%3AComment%3A1264198>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:15
#: 07afd6bd48494ffc8abf1112727bce49
msgid "DIY Drones member Vishnu posted these logs of his X8 plane using APM code 2.73. He described an issue with auto take off where his throttle was maintaining 100% despite being set to 75%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:19
#: bc89ee16946e483c9612a51ebfd350d4
msgid "5/26/2013 tlog file (803 KB) - Downloaded from original blog post \\ `**here** <https://diydrones.com/forum/topics/arduplane-2-73-released?commentId=705844%3AComment%3A1264198>`__. - `x8 throttle slew rate 100 param file <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/other_files/x8throttleslewrate100.param>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:21
#: ce64d751ef834f1db392648258ad3634
msgid "`Jakkur Auto take off and land text file <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/other_files/Jakkur-Auto-take-off-and-land.txt>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:23
#: a073ffdca9754afbbb93ee90aae237f2
msgid "By analyzing this data using :ref:`Mavgraph <mavproxy:mavproxy-mavgraph>`, Tridge was able to provide the following insight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:26
#: 6aa061c74e82432bb4b50d32bb0d8ab1
msgid "***May 29, 2013 DIYDrones; posted to Plane 2.x Software forum:***"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:28
#: 8db0c9c9bd1443debba1d3b3de04ee0c
msgid "\"I've taken a look at your logs, and the biggest problem is that the RLL2SRV_P is not large enough and you have not given Plane enough authority over the turn rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:32
#: 3ec6b185435f4b7b802bb04f06135269
msgid "This is what your flight looked like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:37
#: 723092d4edce4f34bf817a5f0caa78a6
msgid "You can see it did make the first waypoint, but then was turning much too slowly for the second waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:40
#: 366044c54a504f6fbde959523a7e8d9b
msgid "Let's look at a graph of the nav_roll (the roll the plane wants to achieve) and the actual roll. The red line represents the mission sequence number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:47
#: 2103ada407b54a029354a3014a7f7b84
msgid "In the takeoff nav_roll is small, as its flight is straight ahead. It then goes to -30 degrees, as that is the ROLL_LIMIT_DEG you have specified. The problem is that the actual roll only goes to around -10 degrees. So the plane is not achieving the roll that APM is asking for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:52
#: 2c0f35a2eff145718ba45864b444525e
msgid "The reason for this is the RLL2SRV\\_\\* parameters you have chosen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:61
#: 1dd7e52d01b646a7be2647149b1e1fd9
msgid "You have specified zero I term and a quite small P term for an aircraft like the X8. Let's have a look at the servo values that APM ended up using with those settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:68
#: 34dbb15e1839438da4778c3c789a3c10
msgid "You can see that the APM was moving the first elevon only a small amount, and the second elevon by about 150. Now let's compare that to what happened when you switched to manual flight:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:75
#: 286b8ccdfb6e496d8bbdf5340972d522
msgid "When you took manual control you rolled the plane left by 65 degrees. That compares to a maximum roll angle that you have allowed the APM to use of 30 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:79
#: bd20027b98964e36b0c6902849474443
msgid "You also used a lot more aileron movement than you have allowed the APM to use. To roll the plane over you used almost full left aileron, whereas the RLL2SRV_P gain of 0.4 with a 20 degree roll error only allowed the APM to move the aileron by 0.4\\*(20/45)\\*500 which is 89. So you moved the aileron more than 3 times as much as the APM did."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:85
#: a29cf51ecf3f4ce7a72c14ed4cf57b3a
msgid "The X8 has quite a lot of natural stability, which also means it needs quite a lot of elevon movement to get it to roll. If you only move the elevons a small way it will not be able to overcome its natural stability, and also won't overcome any wind, or slight trim errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:90
#: 1472aa1b35fe45369c576e022ba24c40
msgid "To fix it you need to make the following changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:92
#: 97e5c110a94f4386a83637398b1b0d25
msgid "Double your RLL2SRV_P to 0.8, perhaps higher based on testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:93
#: 60ca6c967b894fee9800c7dfc3401abd
msgid "Change RLL2SRV_I to 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:94
#: 5cc383bdee1c45328c45e8a7ececbfc8
msgid "Change RLL2SRV_IMAX to 1500"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:95
#: c8ef0843d98f40a2ad443678a0c4a384
msgid "You also have a value for NAVL1_PERIOD which is too high for an X8. Change it to 18."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:98
#: 82891a94997f42c09ca1e49792c450ca
msgid "Your airspeed also doesn't look well calibrated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/case-study-turn-rate.rst:103
#: fd4b97c4d43043459b039831f9f31e54
msgid "Have you checked your sensor for leaks? It is aligned correctly and clear of the airframe? The airspeed and ground speed should match on average when you loiter. You may need to adjust ARSPD_RATIO to be a bit larger."
msgstr ""
